{"batchcomplete":"","continue":{"gsroffset":6,"continue":"gsroffset||"},"query":{"pages":{"70990980":{"pageid":70990980,"ns":6,"title":"File:1936 Survey of India map of Highlands of Tibet and Surrounding Regions.jpg","index":5,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":107733418,"width":16406,"height":11715,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/1936_Survey_of_India_map_of_Highlands_of_Tibet_and_Surrounding_Regions.jpg/960px-1936_Survey_of_India_map_of_Highlands_of_Tibet_and_Surrounding_Regions.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":457,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/1936_Survey_of_India_map_of_Highlands_of_Tibet_and_Surrounding_Regions.jpg/1280px-1936_Survey_of_India_map_of_Highlands_of_Tibet_and_Surrounding_Regions.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/1936_Survey_of_India_map_of_Highlands_of_Tibet_and_Surrounding_Regions.jpg/960px-1936_Survey_of_India_map_of_Highlands_of_Tibet_and_Surrounding_Regions.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":457,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/1936_Survey_of_India_map_of_Highlands_of_Tibet_and_Surrounding_Regions.jpg/1280px-1936_Survey_of_India_map_of_Highlands_of_Tibet_and_Surrounding_Regions.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/79/1936_Survey_of_India_map_of_Highlands_of_Tibet_and_Surrounding_Regions.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1936_Survey_of_India_map_of_Highlands_of_Tibet_and_Surrounding_Regions.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=70990980","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"A twentieth century masterpiece for the region. This large wall map spans from the Kabul, Delhi and Lucknow, reaching eastward beyond the Mekong, and expanding up beyond the Himalayas to Tashkent, Urumchi and the Gobi desert. With color defining the great sweeping change of elevation that ranges from \"Sea level\" to heights above 28,000 ft. As a practical resource it not only notes place names and boundaries, but railroads, \"roads suitable for wheels\", \"other roads with pass\", \"Telegraph line\", \"Spring\", \"Well\" and even \"Place of archaeological interest. Halting place\". This map once owned by U.S. diplomat, and early climbing enthusiast in the Himalayas, E.M. Groth. He penned his named several times across the canvas backing.\" (Curtis Bird, 2022)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"1936","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.davidrumsey.com/luna/servlet/detail/RUMSEY~8~1~340587~90108839\">https://www.davidrumsey.com/luna/servlet/detail/RUMSEY~8~1~340587~90108839</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\n<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Survey_of_India\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Survey of India\"><span title=\"India's central engineering agency\">Survey of India</span></a></div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},"32396893":{"pageid":32396893,"ns":6,"title":"File:Badaling China Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg","index":1,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":10814543,"width":4184,"height":2680,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Badaling_China_Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg/960px-Badaling_China_Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":410,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Badaling_China_Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg/1280px-Badaling_China_Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Badaling_China_Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg/960px-Badaling_China_Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":410,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Badaling_China_Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg/1280px-Badaling_China_Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/50/Badaling_China_Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Badaling_China_Great-Wall-of-China-01.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=32396893","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Badaling, China: Great Wall of China at Badaling","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"Taken on\u00a03 June 2009","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<span class=\"int-own-work\">Self-photographed</span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Cccefalon\" title=\"User:Cccefalon\">CEphoto, Uwe Aranas</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 3.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 3.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","source":"commons-desc-page"}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},"118882198":{"pageid":118882198,"ns":6,"title":"File:Coral (Favia favus), parque nacional Ras Muhammad, Egipto, 2022-03-27, DD 12.jpg","index":6,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":7944135,"width":3227,"height":3227,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Coral_%28Favia_favus%29%2C_parque_nacional_Ras_Muhammad%2C_Egipto%2C_2022-03-27%2C_DD_12.jpg/960px-Coral_%28Favia_favus%29%2C_parque_nacional_Ras_Muhammad%2C_Egipto%2C_2022-03-27%2C_DD_12.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":640,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Coral_%28Favia_favus%29%2C_parque_nacional_Ras_Muhammad%2C_Egipto%2C_2022-03-27%2C_DD_12.jpg/1280px-Coral_%28Favia_favus%29%2C_parque_nacional_Ras_Muhammad%2C_Egipto%2C_2022-03-27%2C_DD_12.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Coral_%28Favia_favus%29%2C_parque_nacional_Ras_Muhammad%2C_Egipto%2C_2022-03-27%2C_DD_12.jpg/960px-Coral_%28Favia_favus%29%2C_parque_nacional_Ras_Muhammad%2C_Egipto%2C_2022-03-27%2C_DD_12.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":640,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Coral_%28Favia_favus%29%2C_parque_nacional_Ras_Muhammad%2C_Egipto%2C_2022-03-27%2C_DD_12.jpg/1280px-Coral_%28Favia_favus%29%2C_parque_nacional_Ras_Muhammad%2C_Egipto%2C_2022-03-27%2C_DD_12.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/24/Coral_%28Favia_favus%29%2C_parque_nacional_Ras_Muhammad%2C_Egipto%2C_2022-03-27%2C_DD_12.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coral_(Favia_favus),_parque_nacional_Ras_Muhammad,_Egipto,_2022-03-27,_DD_12.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=118882198","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Coral (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Favia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Favia\">Favia favus</a>), <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ras_Muhammad_National_Park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Ras Muhammad National Park\">Ras Muhammad National Park</a>, Red Sea, Egypt. This species of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scleractinia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Scleractinia\">stony corals</a> is massive and forms thickly encrusting dome-shaped <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colony_(biology)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Colony (biology)\">colonial</a> corals. There is a great diversity of form even among the same species. The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/corallite\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:corallite\">corallites</a> project slightly above the surface of the coral and each has its own wall. The septa and costae linked to the corallite wall are well developed and covered by fine teeth. The polyps only extend and feed during the night. Each one has a small number of tapering tentacles which often have a darker coloured tip; these are called stinger tentacles, or sweeper tentacles. They use these to sweep the water to see if any other coral is in its area; if so, then they begin to sting the other coral. This is commonly known as coral war. Each coral is trying to make sure it has enough room around it so it can continue to grow and have more surface area for its offspring.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2022-03-27 09:33:49","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q28147777\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q28147777\"><span title=\"Spanish photographer\">Diego Delso</span></a></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},"107289101":{"pageid":107289101,"ns":6,"title":"File:Khalili Collection Hajj and Arts of Pilgrimage MSS 1288.jpg","index":2,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":58186396,"width":3383,"height":48951,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Khalili_Collection_Hajj_and_Arts_of_Pilgrimage_MSS_1288.jpg/960px-Khalili_Collection_Hajj_and_Arts_of_Pilgrimage_MSS_1288.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":9261,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Khalili_Collection_Hajj_and_Arts_of_Pilgrimage_MSS_1288.jpg/1280px-Khalili_Collection_Hajj_and_Arts_of_Pilgrimage_MSS_1288.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Khalili_Collection_Hajj_and_Arts_of_Pilgrimage_MSS_1288.jpg/960px-Khalili_Collection_Hajj_and_Arts_of_Pilgrimage_MSS_1288.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":9261,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Khalili_Collection_Hajj_and_Arts_of_Pilgrimage_MSS_1288.jpg/1280px-Khali